# Keep the e2e/Dockerfile build context (repo root) lean. The image only needs:
#   - e2e/                          (Dockerfile + harness scripts)
#   - android-app/                  (Gradle project, for the offline gradle-home prime)
#   - e2e/target-app/               (Gradle project, for the prime)
#   - e2e/draw-app/                 (Gradle project, for the prime)
#   - porting/vendor/sdl-android-java (SDL Java glue android-app's sourceSets reference)
# Everything else (submodules, native build trees, artifacts, git) is mounted at
# runtime via -v "$REPO_ROOT:/workspace" — it must NOT bloat the build context.
.git
ai
ios-cmake
screenshots
scrcpy
scrcpy-app
scrcpy-ios
external
output
README.md
LICENSE
Makefile

# Native build trees / outputs / artifacts (build artifacts, never in the image).
porting/build
porting/libs
porting/output
e2e/artifacts

# Only porting/vendor/sdl-android-java is needed from porting/ — exclude the rest
# of porting/ (cmake, scripts, src, etc.) from the context. The COPY in the
# Dockerfile pulls just porting/vendor/sdl-android-java.
porting/cmake
porting/scripts
porting/src
porting/include
porting/patches

# Local gradle state / staged artifacts (regenerated at runtime).
**/.gradle
**/build
android-app/app/src/main/jniLibs
android-app/app/src/main/assets/scrcpy-server
**/local.properties
